      "content": "If you feel specific external triggers correlate with your mistakes, focus intensely on establishing unwavering consistency in your core routines. Implement \"pre-mortem\" planning for the riskiest parts of your day, where you anticipate potential failures and plan specific countermeasures beforehand. For small tasks, use detailed checklists and set digital reminders 10-15 minutes *before* deadlines to ensure you are always ahead of the curve. This meticulous approach optimizes for error prevention rather than reacting to perceived scrutiny.",
